+# ChatGPT AI DM — campaign bootstrap
+
+Why a "new campaign" can look broken in the UI, and what the MCP client should do instead.
+
+## What you saw
+
+Asking ChatGPT to *start a new campaign* may produce **one line in Recent Events** (from `record_event`) but nothing else on the dashboard — no open session, no new plots, no world entries.
+
+That is expected if the model only called `record_event`. Events are a **timeline**, not the world graph.
+
+## What actually gets stored where
+
+| What | Tool | Shows in UI as |
+|------|------|----------------|
+| Opening pitch / "what happened" beat | `record_event` | Recent events |
+| Play session | `start_session` | Open session card |
+| Locations, NPCs, factions, plots | `propose_world_update` → `commit_world_update` | Active plots, World browser |
+| Facts on entities | `add_fact` in world update | Search / entity detail |
+| Bulk notes | `import_campaign_markdown` → commit | World browser |
+
+## Required bootstrap sequence (AI DM)
+
+The MCP server returns these steps in **`instructions`** on `initialize` (system-level guidance for ChatGPT). Summary:
+
+1. `start_session`
+2. `propose_world_update` — at minimum: starting **location**, one **plot** (`status: active`), PC/party **npc** entities, key **facts**
+3. `commit_world_update` — immediately (ChatGPT has no approval queue)
+4. `record_event` — optional, for the opening beat
+5. `get_campaign_dashboard` — verify before narrating
+
+## Resume flow
+
+1. `prepare_session_brief` or `get_campaign_dashboard`
+2. `start_session` if none open
+3. `compile_scene_context` before the next scene
+
+## Hosted prod note
+
+Production uses `campaign_001` with optional demo seed (Blackport). A "new" campaign adds entities alongside that data until we ship per-user campaigns or a reset tool. The dashboard title may still say the seed name until campaign metadata is updated.
+
+## Code
+
+- Instructions: `web/app/Services/WorldKeep/Mcp/Instructions.php`
+- Tool blurbs: `web/app/Services/WorldKeep/Mcp/ToolDefinitions.php`
+
+After changing instructions, redeploy so ChatGPT re-initializes the connector.
